  "title": "The garbage compactor",
  "section": "Movie Facts # 4 of 10",
  "description": "Star Wars was originally slated for release in Christmas 1976; however, delays pushed the film's debut to summer 1977. Already anxious about meeting his deadline, George Lucas was stunned when his original film editor's first cut was a \"complete disaster.\" Paul Hirsh, Richard Chew, and Lucas' then-wife Marcia Lucas (cutting Martin Scorsese's New York, New York at the time) were called in to re-shape the movie. Chew found that conventional cutting had given Star Wars a non-energetic pace. He and an equally-rushed Hirsh worked on two reels simultaneously; whoever finished first would then move on to the next."
